Yes, 14 Mill Wynd is within the **Glenarrow Town Centre conservation area**. It is not a listed building and has no tree preservation order.

Under the council's windows guidance, replacing windows in a conservation area needs a planning application unless the new windows match the existing ones in material and pattern. So if you want to change the material (for example, timber to uPVC) or the design (for example, the glazing bar pattern or opening style), you will likely need to apply first.

I can't give a formal opinion on your specific proposal. If you'd like, tell me the existing and proposed window details and I can point you to the relevant guidance. You can also contact the planning desk to confirm whether your scheme needs an application before you start work.
